.TH MESHWAV-AGENT 1 "" "meshwav-agent" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
meshwav-agent \- stream this computer's audio to a paired phone over Tailscale
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B meshwav-agent
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B meshwav-agent
.RB { devices | pair | use " \fIDEVICE\fR|auto" | rename " \fIDEVICE NEWNAME\fR }"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Captures the system audio with parec, encodes it (Opus, or lossless PCM) and sends it, encrypted, over UDP to a paired receiver on the tailnet.
While a receiver is connected the default output is redirected to a virtual sink, so this computer plays nothing locally. It is handed back when the receiver leaves and when the agent exits.
The agent only listens on a tailnet or loopback address.
.PP
Run it as a user service: \fBsystemctl --user enable --now meshwav-agent\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
These talk to the running agent over an owner-only socket (\fI~/.config/meshwav/control.sock\fR).
.TP
.B devices
List paired devices: online, active or standby.
.TP
.B pair
Open a 2-minute pairing window and print a 6-digit code for the app.
.TP
.BR use " \fIDEVICE\fR|auto"
Send the audio to one device (name, name prefix or key prefix). \fBauto\fR lets the first connected device keep it.
.TP
.BR rename " \fIDEVICE NEWNAME\fR"
Rename a paired device.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " IP:PORT"
Address to listen on (default: tailscale IPv4, port 47900).
.TP
.BI \-\-kbps " N"
Opus bitrate, 64\-256 (default 160).
.TP
.BI \-\-frame\-ms " N"
Opus frame size: 5, 10 or 20 (default 10).
.TP
.BI \-\-source " SINK.monitor"
Capture from this source and do not redirect.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-redirect
Leave the local audio output alone.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Settings file (default \fI~/.config/meshwav/config.toml\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " LEVEL"
error, warn, info or debug.
.TP
.B \-\-pair
Open a pairing window at start-up.
.TP
.BI \-\-identity " PATH" ", " \-\-authorized " PATH"
Key and paired-device files.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/meshwav/config.toml
Flat key = value settings: bind, kbps, frame_ms, source, no_redirect, log_level. See \fI/usr/share/doc/meshwav-agent/config.toml.example\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/meshwav/{identity,authorized_peers,active_peer}
The agent's key, the paired devices and the chosen device.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/tech-house-blr/meshwav
